GRAPH <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_SelfDescribingArchivePreservesMeaning> {
  <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Digest_Narrative_SelfDescribingArchivePreservesMeaning> a narr:Digest ;
    narr:digestOf <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Narrative_SelfDescribingArchivePreservesMeaning> ;
    narr:childCount "10"^^xsd:integer ;
    narr:generatedFrom "88e36c162aa3ba30a94074c3b2f7b68fbe13aefc" ;
    narr:narration """This narrative gathers the case for extracting closed legacy records into an open, self-describing archive rather than leaving them on a decommissioned-but-alive platform. [The problem statement](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_3) sets the stakes: eleven years of closed history stays behind on the old platform while only open work migrates. [The rejection of the read-only fallback](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7) argues a system nobody patches fails quietly, discovered only when a claim needs an old record. [The core proposal](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9) is extraction into flat files with schema and field-meaning documentation, and [the concrete spec](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_11) insists on readability in ten years with nothing but the files — no vendor engine, no proprietary export. [The semantic-decay thesis](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13) holds that the data is easy to keep but the meaning rots, and [the structural objection](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15) names why this never gets done: cost now against risk landing on someone absent. [A second rationale](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16) adds the behavioral argument — an obviously-an archive prevents a dual system of record — which [Xavier concedes is stronger than his own](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_17). [The consolidated position](narr:Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_22) ties switch-off timing, extraction-first sequencing, and written legal retention sign-off into one decision.""" ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_11> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_12> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_17> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_22> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_3> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7> ;
    narr:covers <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9> ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "We do not keep the legacy platform alive as a read-only system. We extract the closed history into a flat, self-describing archive" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Flat files, an open format, a schema next to them, and a written description of what a \"consignment status of 7\" actually meant in 2017" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_11> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "The data is easy to keep. The meaning is what rots." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "Cost and effort now, against a risk that lands years from now on someone who isn't in this room." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "If Ferry Road can still look something up in the old system, someone at Ferry Road will, and then we've got two systems of record for a year." ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16> ] ;
    narr:keyPhrase [ narr:text "the retention period comes from legal in writing before we sign anything with the vendor about decommissioning" ; narr:phraseSource <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_22> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The read-only legacy platform was the live alternative before being argued down as expensive and fragile — a road not taken someone might still reach for." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_7> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_9> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "Two distinct justifications coexist — semantic decay versus behavioral dual-record risk — and the speakers themselves rank the behavioral one stronger." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_13> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_16> ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_17> ] ;
    narr:variation [ narr:text "The structural counter-argument (cost now, deferred risk, why it never gets done) is voiced inside the supporting side as the standing obstacle, not resolved away." ; narr:over <https://aswritten.ai/narrative#Expr_5HalyardLegacyArchive20260922_15> ] ;
    narr:writer "z-ai/glm-5.3-flash:nitro" .
}